    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"[Graph.layout_shell()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-method}\"\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\ntoc-depth: 3\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nPlace the nodes on concentric circles (shells).\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L4539-L4695){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-Kind.FUNCTION}\n```python\nGraph.layout_shell(\n    nlist=None,\n    rotate=None,\n    scale=1.0,\n    center=(0.0, 0.0),\n    attr_name=None,\n    return_dict=False,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Shell layout](/assets/graphs/layout-shell.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"On the left, a ten-node graph scattered at random, its nodes colored by their shell attribute: a hub in the accent color, its three neighbors in teal and six outer nodes in violet, two on each neighbor. On the right, layout_shell(nlist='shell') puts the hub at the center, its neighbors on a small circle around it and the outer nodes on a larger circle outside.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\n`nlist=` splits the nodes into shells, innermost first. Shell `k` (of `s` shells) has\nradius `k * scale / s`, counting from `1`, except that a first shell holding a single\nnode puts that node at the center and the next shell at radius `scale / s`. Nodes are\nspread evenly around their shell, and each shell starts `rotate=` radians further round\nthan the one inside it, so neighboring shells don't line up. This matches NetworkX's\n`shell_layout()`.\n\nShell layouts show a hierarchy or a grouping: a hub surrounded by its neighbors,\nk-cores from the dense center outward, or nodes grouped by type. With `nlist=None`\nevery node goes on one circle (like `layout_circular()`, but starting at the `rotate=`\nangle).\n\nPositions are stored as `[x, y]` lists in the `attr_name=` node attribute; see\n`layout_circular()`.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[nlist]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[Union[list, str]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   The shells, innermost first, as a list of lists of node IDs or labels, or the name\n    of a node attribute to group by: nodes sharing a value form a shell, with shells in\n    sorted value order and nodes in ID order. Every node must be in exactly one shell.\n    If `None` (default), all nodes form one shell, in ID order.\n\n<code>[rotate]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[float]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Angle, in radians, by which each shell is turned relative to the previous one; the\n    first shell starts at this angle too. If `None` (default), uses `pi / s` for `s`\n    shells.\n\n<code>[scale]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [float]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[1.0]{.fl}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Sets the spacing of the shells, which are `scale / s` apart: the outermost shell has\n    radius `scale`, or `(s - 1) * scale / s` when the first shell is a single node at the\n    center. Default is `1.0`.\n\n<code>[center]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [tuple[float, float]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [(0.0, 0.0)]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Center of the shells, as `(x, y)`. Default is the origin.\n\n<code>[attr_name]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Node attribute to store the positions in. If `None` (default), uses `\"pos\"`.\n\n<code>[return_dict]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[False]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, returns a dictionary instead of self. If `False` (default), stores the\n    positions on the nodes and returns self for chaining.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Union[dict[int, tuple[float, float]], Graph]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `return_dict=` is `True`: dictionary mapping node IDs to `(x, y)` tuples. If\n    `return_dict=` is `False` (default): returns self for method chaining.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If a node is missing from `nlist=` or appears in more than one shell, a node in\n    `nlist=` doesn't exist, the named attribute is missing on some node, or `scale=` or\n    `center=` is invalid.\n:::\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nA star with its hub in the middle and the leaves around it:\n\n::: {#c56f2dca .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph().add_star_graph(5)\n\npos = graph.layout_shell(nlist=[[1], [2, 3, 4, 5]], return_dict=True)\n{nid: (round(x, 3), round(y, 3)) for nid, (x, y) in pos.items()}\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n{1: (0.0, 0.0), 2: (-0.5, 0.0), 3: (-0.0, -0.5), 4: (0.5, -0.0), 5: (0.0, 0.5)}\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nGrouping by an attribute: the k-core number puts the densest core in the middle:\n\n::: {#9a2f2860 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\n(\n    ec.karate_club()\n    .coreness(attr_name=\"core\")\n    .layout_shell(nlist=\"core\")\n    .plot(layout=\"pos\", color_by=\"core\", show_labels=False)\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<div style=\"position:relative;display:inline-block\">\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"600\" height=\"400\" viewBox=\"110.2 17.4 379.6 365.2\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<rect x=\"110.2\" y=\"17.4\" width=\"379.6\" height=\"365.2\" fill=\"#fafafa\"/>\n<path d=\"M336.2,209.6 C330.1,211.0 313.4,221.0 299.4,217.6 C285.3,214.2 274.4,192.5 252.1,189.4 C229.7,186.2 179.8,197.1 165.3,198.7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"0.96\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"22-1-0\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<path d=\"M336.7,211.1 C327.0,214.4 289.7,225.0 278.6,231.2 C267.6,237.3 279.7,244.3 270.5,248.0 C261.2,251.8 236.3,248.4 223.1,253.5 C209.8,258.6 196.2,274.5 190.8,278.8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"0.96\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"22-2-1\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<line x1=\"247.1\" y1=\"329.8\" x2=\"160.2\" y2=\"210.2\" stroke=\"#f28e2c\" stroke-width=\"0.96\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"3-1-2\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<line x1=\"244.3\" y1=\"332.6\" x2=\"191.1\" y2=\"293.9\" stroke=\"#f28e2c\" stroke-width=\"0.96\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"3-2-3\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<line x1=\"267.1\" y1=\"340.0\" x2=\"332.9\" y2=\"340.0\" stroke=\"#f28e2c\" stroke-width=\"0.96\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"3-4-4\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<line x1=\"266.5\" y1=\"336.1\" x2=\"407.1\" y2=\"290.4\" stroke=\"#f28e2c\" stroke-width=\"0.96\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"3-8-5\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<path d=\"M263.5,331.2 C272.1,322.7 299.1,293.2 315.1,280.6 C331.0,267.9 344.0,262.0 359.0,255.2 C374.1,248.3 392.0,247.4 405.1,239.6 C418.3,231.9 432.6,213.8 438.0,208.6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#f28e2c\" stroke-width=\"0.96\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"3-9-6\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<path d=\"M255.3,327.4 C255.6,321.3 255.2,304.8 257.5,290.7 C259.8,276.6 264.8,258.8 269.1,243.0 C273.3,227.2 278.